<div>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"direction:ltr;text-align:left;text-indent:0=
px;text-transform:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">Hi</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">I received an offline comment from a senior IETF participant suggesting t=
hat I had misunderstood the draft and that the key reuse in question referr=
ed to reuse within a single
 session. That is not accurate. The draft talks about static keys, i.e., ke=
ys used in more than one key-establishment.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">Given the apparent confusion between 1. reuse of ephemeral keys within a =
session, 2. reuse of ephemeral keys across sessions, and 3. static keys, ea=
ch of which carries distinct
 privacy and security implications, I recommend that the AD ensure that all=
 not yet published drafts use very precise terminology. Specifically, a key=
 used in more than one key-establishment should use the well-established te=
rm =E2=80=9Cstatic key=E2=80=9D.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">---</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">1. Reuse of ephemeral keys within a session:</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">- Session A: ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry1 and X25519MLKEM768 =
KeyShareEntry2 both containing the same ML-KEM public key.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">2. Reuse of ephemeral keys across sessions:</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">- Session B1. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry3 and X25519 KeyShar=
eEntry4. Sever picks X25519 KeyShareEntry4.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">- Session B2. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry3 and X25519 KeyShar=
eEntry5.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">3. Static keys</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">- Session C1. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry6. Sever picks MLKEM=
768 KeyShareEntry6</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">- Session C2. ClientHello with MLKEM768 KeyShareEntry6. Sever picks MLKEM=
768 KeyShareEntry6</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">---</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">Issues with the text on static keys were clearly raised during the first =
WGLC and should have been addressed before the second. Having to repeat the=
 same issues is both frustrating
 and a waste of time.<br>
<br>
The major issues, that the draft lacks proper security considerations for t=
he use of static keys (they should be quite negative), and that it does not=
 explain how an implementation using static keys can be conformant with NIS=
T specifications, were raised during
 the first WGLC and have not been addressed. During the second WGLC, it was=
 identified that conformance is intrinsically linked to the patent license.=
</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">My constructive suggestion is to remove all text regarding static keys, a=
s there is no reason for this draft to include them. I do not believe compa=
risons with draft-ietf-tls-hybrid-design
 are relevant, since that document serves a completely different purpose an=
d does not register code points.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">If the draft intends to retain any text on static keys, NIST SP 1800-37,
<i>Addressing Visibility Challenges with TLS 1.3 within the Enterprise</i>,=
 is a useful reference regarding the negative privacy and security implicat=
ions of static keys. I do not have specific guidance on how to achieve conf=
ormance with NIST specifications
 when using static keys, but that issue must clearly be resolved.</span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">I do not find any text in RFC 8446 that allows the use of static keys. If=
 the TLS WG intends to explicitly permit static keys again, their use shoul=
d be explicitly negotiated,
 as done in TLS 1.2 or draft-rhrd-tls-tls13-visibility.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">As I have seen no response from the authors indicating that they plan to =
address this issue, I am opposed to publishing this document.</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">=C2=A0</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">Cheers,</span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal" style=3D"text-align:left;text-indent:0px;text-transf=
orm:none;margin:0cm">
<span style=3D"font-family:Aptos,sans-serif;font-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)=
">John</span></p>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt;color:rgb(0,0,0)">
<br>
</div>
<div id=3D"m_-5050180461578459232mail-editor-reference-message-container">
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
</div>
<div style=3D"text-align:left;padding:3pt 0in 0in;border-width:1pt medium m=
edium;border-style:solid none none;border-color:rgb(181,196,223) currentcol=
or currentcolor;font-family:Aptos;font-size:12pt;color:black">
<b>From: </b>Russ Housley &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:housley@vigilsec.com" targe=
t=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">housley@vigilsec.com</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Date: </b>Thursday, 12 February 2026 at 22:38<br>
<b>To: </b>Joseph Salowey &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:joe@salowey.net" target=3D"=
_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">joe@salowey.net</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Cc: </b><u></u>
<div style=3D"text-align:left">
&lt;<a href=3D"mailto:tls@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">tl=
s@ietf.org</a>&gt;, John Mattsson &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:john.mattsson@erics=
son.com" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">john.mattsson@ericsson.com</a=
>&gt;<br>
<b>Subject: </b>Re: [TLS] WG Last Call: draft-ietf-tls-mlkem-05 (Ends 2026-=
02-27)<br>
<br>
</div>
<u></u></div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
I support the publication of this document as an RFC.=C2=A0 I would prefer =
to have the clarity about ephemeral vs. static ML-KEM keys as posted by Joh=
n Mattsson, but I can live with it as-is.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
Russ</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
<br>
</div>
<blockquote>
<div>On Feb 12, 2026, at 3:08=E2=80=AFPM, John Mattsson &lt;john.mattsson=
=3D<a href=3D"mailto:40ericsson.com@dmarc.ietf.org" target=3D"_blank" rel=
=3D"noreferrer">40ericsson.com@dmarc.ietf.org</a>&gt; wrote:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
Hi,</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
I support publication iff all text related to =E2=80=9Ckey reuse=E2=80=9D i=
s removed. In its current form, I do not believe -07 should be published.</=
div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
Major Comments:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
- FIPS 203 states that:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
=E2=80=9Cthe licensed patents be freely available to be practiced by any im=
plementer of the ML-KEM algorithm as published by NIST.=E2=80=9D</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
=E2=80=9Crequirements for the secure use of KEMs in applications, see SP 80=
0-227.=E2=80=9D</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
A reused key is, by definition, a static key. SP 800-227 imposes additional=
 requirements for static keys compared to ephemeral keys. The draft does no=
t explain how an implementer can satisfy these requirements. This creates p=
otential non-conformance with NIST
 specifications.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
- =C2=A0The draft does not describe the significant security and privacy pr=
oblems associated with key reuse. IND-CCA is a theoretical property of the =
algorithm. However, the security and privacy problems=C2=A0are related to t=
he reuse of keys in the TLS 1.3 protocol in
 deployments.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
Minor Comments:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
- The discussion of randomness reuse in ciphertexts and references to SP 80=
0-227 do not belong in a =E2=80=9Ckey reuse=E2=80=9D section. Ciphertexts a=
re not keys, and SP 800-227 contains broader guidelines and requirements be=
yond static keys.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
- =E2=80=9CThe client&#39;s shares are listed in descending order of client=
 preference; the server selects one algorithm and sends its corresponding s=
hare.=E2=80=9D</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
The server may also select no share and respond with a handshake_failure or=
 a HelloRetryRequest (HRR). Since this is already specified in RFC 8446, it=
 would be better to remove this text and simply reference RFC 8446.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
- Section 5.1 appears to =E2=80=8Bmix different concepts: hybrids, PQ/T hyb=
rids, and lattice-based PQ/T hybrids. I assume the person asking for this s=
ection wanted a comparison with [ECDHE-MLKEM]. I suggest doing that. In the=
 future, PQ/T hybrids will likely become
 less common, but it is unclear whether other hybrids (e.g., ML-KEM + HQC-K=
EM) will gain adoption.</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
Cheers,</div>
<div style=3D"font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;font-size:12pt">
John</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;font-family:Aptos,Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;fo=
nt-size:12pt">
<br>
</div>
<div id=3D"m_-5050180461578459232mail-editor-reference-message-container">
<div style=3D"padding:3pt 0in 0in;border-width:1pt medium medium;border-sty=
le:solid none none;border-color:rgb(181,196,223) currentcolor currentcolor"=
>
<div style=3D"text-align:left;font-family:Aptos;font-size:12pt">
<b>From: </b>Joseph Salowey &lt;<a href=3D"mailto:joe@salowey.net" target=
=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">joe@salowey.net</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Date: </b>Thursday, 12 February 2026 at 20:06<br>
<b>To:</b></div>
<div style=3D"text-align:left;font-family:Aptos;font-size:12pt">
&lt;<a href=3D"mailto:tls@ietf.org" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">tl=
s@ietf.org</a>&gt;<br>
<b>Subject: </b>[TLS] WG Last Call: draft-ietf-tls-mlkem-05 (Ends 2026-02-2=
7)<br>
<br>
</div>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;font-family:&quot=
;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
This message starts the second Working Group Last Call for the pure ML-KEM =
document (draft-ietf-tls-mlkem-07).</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;min-height:15px;f=
ont-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;font-family:&quot=
;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
The file can be retrieved from:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;font-family:&quot=
;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
<a href=3D"https://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-mlkem/" style=3D=
"margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px" target=3D"_blank" rel=3D"noreferrer">htt=
ps://datatracker.ietf.org/doc/draft-ietf-tls-mlkem/</a><br>
<br>
The diff with the previous WGLC draft (-05) is here:</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;min-height:15px;f=
ont-family:&quot;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
<br>
</div>
<div style=3D"direction:ltr;line-height:normal;margin:0px;font-family:&quot=
;Helvetica Neue&quot;;font-size:13px">
<a href=3D"https://author-tools.ietf.org/iddiff?url1=3Ddraft-ietf-tls-mlkem=
